commit ee673d6a71d76e67b532dc7eaf91d92edc3bb8bb
Author: Christopher Webb <207731778+thechriswebb@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Tue Sep 22 14:45:38 2026 -0500

    Extract the model cache and stop whole-cache eviction abandoning an in-flight load (#603)
    
    * Move the model cache into its own file
    
    - Moves the constraint kind, the tokenizer bias, and the cache actor out of the model file, changing only the access the cross-file use requires: `private actor ModelCache` becomes `actor ModelCache`, because a `private` top-level type is visible only inside its own file. No other content changes.
    
    The model cache grew large enough inside MLXLanguageModel.swift to warrant its own file, separate from the model's own responsibilities.
    
    * Catch only the fork-unavailable error when a constraint clone fails
    
    - Narrows the freshly-compiled constraint's clone attempt from a blanket `try?` to a catch on `GrammarError.forkFailed`, matching the cached-template clone site above it, which already narrowed this way. Every other clone failure now reaches the caller instead of being silently treated as the expected one.
    
    A blanket `try?` treated every clone failure as the one expected case, xgrammar lacking `Fork()`. `GrammarConstraint.clone()` has exactly one throw site today, so this narrowing changes no observable behavior yet; it only stops a future second failure mode from being swallowed the same way.
    
    * Cancel every registered load from evictAll()
    
    - Cancels every registered load task, which remove(modelID:) already did for one model.
    - Corrects the eviction documentation, which claimed an in-flight load completes.
    - Adds a test that evictAll() cancels an in-flight load, and the same probe against evict().
    - Bounds both new tests with a time limit, because each parks its loader and a regression would hang.
    
    evictAll() dropped every load registration without cancelling, so nothing in the process could reach a load that was still running. A caller awaiting preload() or respond() now fails, and callers coalesced onto one load fail together. Cancellation is cooperative. A load already inside loadWeights runs to completion and allocates, and that limit applies to evict() too.
    
    * Rename the grammar tokenizer members away from an xgrammar abbreviation
    
    - Renames the grammar tokenizer members and their storage away from an abbreviation of the library name: `xgTokenizers` becomes `grammarTokenizers`, `makeXGTokenizer` becomes `makeGrammarTokenizer`, and `hasCachedXGTokenizer` becomes `hasCachedGrammarTokenizer`, at every call site.
    - Renames the same local variables at every call site: `xgTokenizer` and `xgTok` become `grammarTokenizer`, and the `vocab` local inside `makeGrammarTokenizer` becomes `vocabulary` to avoid shadowing the `vocab:` parameter label once its neighbor is renamed.
    
    The cache's tokenizer members were named after xgrammar's own abbreviation rather than the type they store, which the style guide's initialism rule flags.
    
    * Name the download progress throughput property in full
    
    - Renames the observable throughput property to throughputBytesPerSecond, dropping the abbreviation.
    - Drops public from the two reporting entry points, leaving the observable state and the shared instance public.
    
    Every caller of the two entry points is in this module, and the tests reach them through @testable import, so neither needs to be public. No release contains this type: the newest tag is 3.31.4 from June, and the whole MLXFoundationModels library arrived in July, so no consumer can depend on either name.
    
    * Track download progress for each model
    
    - Keys the progress state on the model ID, with one published value per model and accessors that add every entry.
    - Reports the end of a load from a defer, so a failed or cancelled load clears its own entry.
    - Sends every report through one stream and one main-actor consumer, which applies them in the order the loader sent them.
    - Gives every load its own identifier, so a report from a cancelled load cannot change the load that replaced it.
    - Removes isActive and modelName, and adds activeDownloads and download(forModelID:).
    
    One fraction and one identifier cannot describe two loads, and the cache loads models concurrently, so two downloads overwrote each other's state. reportCompleted() ran only after a successful load, so a cancelled load left the state active for the life of the process. Each report also created its own main-actor task, and those tasks run in no fixed order, so a progress report could apply after the end and leave a finished download on screen. Eviction cancels a load and forgets it at once, so a replacement can start while the cancelled load still transfers bytes, and both shared one entry.
    
    No release contains this type, so none of these changes can break a consumer.

